WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:06.833
If you were asked to take this training, you lead at least one US non-exempt employee.

00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:10.026
Your review is what keeps their timecards accurate.

00:00:11.376 --> 00:00:19.794
To confirm, open the team member's profile in Workday, select the Position tab, and read FLSA Exemption Status.

00:00:19.794 --> 00:00:23.131
No, eligible for overtime, means non-exempt.

00:00:24.481 --> 00:00:26.952
You also manage on-call eligibility.

00:00:26.952 --> 00:00:31.414
Use the manager section of the global on-call article in Workday.

00:00:32.764 --> 00:00:38.161
Make sure your team completes this training, and knows the program, the resources, and the process.

00:00:39.511 --> 00:00:44.436
Timecards with only regular hours are approved automatically at submission.

00:00:44.436 --> 00:00:45.355
Review anyway.

00:00:45.355 --> 00:00:49.623
Make it a ritual, and check that the reported hours are accurate.

00:00:50.973 --> 00:00:53.629
If something is wrong, do not use Send Back.

00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:55.018
Talk with the employee.

00:00:55.018 --> 00:00:59.123
A conversation makes the correction clear, and builds better habits.

00:01:00.473 --> 00:01:07.469
Follow up immediately when Workday alerts you that a part-time employee or intern has not entered time.

00:01:07.469 --> 00:01:14.873
Also resolve overlap alerts: hours worked against time off, and on-call standby against on-call hours worked.

00:01:16.223 --> 00:01:23.177
Encourage the team to take required rest and meal breaks, and use one-to-ones to talk through schedules and discrepancies.

00:01:24.527 --> 00:01:32.954
Always assign a delegate to approve on your behalf, including for an unscheduled absence, extended time off, or a leave of absence.

00:01:34.304 --> 00:01:37.385
Your hard stop is Sunday at 6:30 PM Pacific.

00:01:37.385 --> 00:01:42.005
Use Explore the Week in this lesson for every deadline in between.
